<%#
  The one and only render of a freshly minted set of recovery codes
  (CHARTER §6 phase 4). Reached by POSTing the regenerate verb; there is no
  redirect, because a redirect would carry the codes in a flash and a flash
  is a cookie. Nothing here is stored: admin_actions recorded how many codes
  were made, never which.
%>
<h2>New recovery codes</h2>
<p class="footnote">Account <code><%= @account_id %></code> &middot; <%= @target %></p>

<div class="degraded">
  <p><strong>Copy these now.</strong> This page is the only time they are shown. They are in the authdb, but this tool
    will never display them again and reloading this page will not bring them back.</p>
  <p>The account&rsquo;s previous codes were deleted when these were minted, and reloading this page does not
    re-show these: it re-POSTs the verb and mints another set, which invalidates the ones above.</p>
</div>

<table>
  <tr><th>Recovery code</th></tr>
  <% @codes.each do |code| %>
    <tr><td><code><%= code %></code></td></tr>
  <% end %>
</table>

<p class="footnote">Hand them to the customer over a channel you have already authenticated them on. The old codes are
  gone: anything they wrote down before now no longer works.</p>

<p><a href="<%= account_path(@account_id) %>">&larr; back to the account</a></p>
